{
  "format": 1,
  "note": "Surface recipes of the nine weapons (Toolgen 0.13 Enamel) and the scout rifle (0.24, sheet 11 from its weapon spec KG11), source: Cube Escape Docs/EQUIPMENT.md > Zielbild > Texturen 1-9 (concept sheet weapon_textures_1-9.webp, 16.10.2026). 'recipe' goes into the contract (surface.recipe, a proposal for Cube Escape's presets: material kind, smoothness, wear, glow per channel); Toolgen bakes only 'relief' (normal map) and the decals (weapon_designs.py DECALS). Relief keys select the parts of a weapon: a glob on the source part name without the SM_PG_ prefix, or '@<Channel>' for every part of that channel; the first matching key wins; a value is one pattern or a list of patterns that add up. Sizes in mm in the tool frame (Socket_Hand; forward -y, up +z, lateral x). Height of every pattern 0..1 x strength x limits.max_height_mm.",
  "limits": {"max_height_mm": 0.3, "smoothness_max": 0.45, "wear_levels": {"subtle": 0.2, "medium": 0.5, "strong": 0.8}},
  "patterns": {
    "knurl": "diamond knurling: two families of grooves at +-45 degrees between 'direction' and 'across'; size_mm = pitch",
    "grooves": "round corrugation repeating along 'direction' (the grooves run across it); size_mm = pitch",
    "lamellae": "flat ribs with gaps repeating along 'direction'; size_mm = pitch",
    "seams": "narrow panel joints (width_mm) every size_mm along 'direction', a second family along 'across' when 'across_mm' is set; pressed in",
    "brushed": "fine streaks running along 'direction' (anisotropic noise, size_mm = streak width)",
    "grain": "isotropic fine grain (ceramic, cast metal), size_mm = feature size"
  },
